From 68dd42c4a6cc4975b9cf6c14bd0ffcaacde2ab9d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: t <t@t>
Date: Fri, 30 Oct 2026 23:10:18 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 14/16] ASoC: qcom: audioreach: add closed-loop speaker
 protection support

The speaker protection module of the DSP needs its calibration set, a
control link to the voltage/current module, the resistance and
temperature of each speaker, and its fault event. The driver sends none
of this.

Add a loader for two optional firmware files, one with the control links
and calibration records of the model and one with the R0/T0 of the unit,
both generated locally. Declare the control links in GRAPH_OPEN, in the
graph that holds the owner module of a link. Send the calibration records
of each module with the media format, send R0/T0
(PARAM_ID_SP_TH_VI_R0T0_CFG)
after a range check against the nominal resistance, and register the
speaker protection diagnostics event. Report the loaded data, the
closed-loop graph, the sense streams and the calibration to the speaker
protection guard, and latch a fault on any diagnostics event, because the
payload is not decoded. The guard counts a graph once per run: report
only the first start and the last stop of a graph.

The loaded data is reference counted, so the calibration file is read and
the DSP commands are sent without holding the lock that protects the
pointer, and the data is freed when the driver goes away.

Without the first file nothing changes. Without the second file the
guard keeps the speakers muted. The speaker protection guard is selected
by the AudioReach core, so it cannot be a module for a built-in core.

Assisted-by: Claude Sonnet 5.5
